   "role": "system",
   "text": "You are playing BLINDBOARD, a deduction game about a hidden keyboard.\n\nTHE BOARD\nThe board is a one-handed keyboard with 12 keys: 4 fingers (pinky, ring, middle, index) x 3 rows (top, home, bottom). Each key is addressed by finger and row. The complete list of valid key addresses:\nL-pinky-top, L-pinky-home, L-pinky-bottom, L-ring-top, L-ring-home, L-ring-bottom, L-middle-top, L-middle-home, L-middle-bottom, L-index-top, L-index-home, L-index-bottom\n\nThe 12 symbols A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K, L are assigned to the 12 keys in a hidden arrangement (each symbol on exactly one key). Your job: work out which symbol is on which key.\n\nEACH TURN\n- You press exactly 3 DIFFERENT keys (a chord) by giving their addresses.\n- Next turn you are told which 3 symbols those keys held, as an ALPHABETICALLY SORTED list. You are NOT told which symbol came from which key. Overlap your chords cleverly to pin symbols to keys.\n\nROTATIONS\nAfter your presses each turn, some keys may be ROTATED: the letters on the rotated keys are rearranged among those same keys, and every rotated key ends up with a different letter than it had (the set of letters on those keys is unchanged; only their places among those keys change). Next turn you are told exactly WHICH keys were rotated, but not how they were rearranged. Rotations become rarer as the game goes on and eventually stop.\n\nLOCKS (optional, side score)\nOn any press turn you may lock letters onto keys you are sure of: +1 point if correct at that moment, -3 if wrong. You get no feedback on locks during the game. Each key can be locked only once, ever.\n\nFINAL GUESS\nYou may end the game at any time by submitting your full guess. After turn 18 you MUST submit it. Your main score is how many of the 12 keys you guess correctly, judged against the arrangement at the moment you guess.\n\nRESPONSE FORMAT\nReply with ONLY one JSON object, no other text.\nTo press: {\"presses\": [\"L-pinky-top\", \"L-ring-home\", \"L-middle-bottom\"]}\nTo press and lock: {\"presses\": [ ... 3 addresses ... ], \"locks\": {\"L-pinky-home\": \"A\"}}\nTo guess (ends the game): {\"guess\": {\"L-pinky-top\": \"A\", ... one entry for every key ...}}"
